      en: "The Sichuan Basin in southwest China is a fertile red sandstone basin encircled by mountains. Covering 260,000 square kilometers, it is one of China's most populous regions, with over 100 million residents. The humid subtropical climate and rich alluvial soils support intensive agriculture, especially rice, wheat, and citrus. The Dujiangyan irrigation system, built in 256 BCE, still irrigates over 5,300 square kilometers of farmland. Chengdu, the capital, is a major industrial and tech center. The basin is also the primary habitat of the giant panda.",
