      en: "The Tian Shan Mountains span 2,500 km across Central Asia, mainly in Kyrgyzstan, Kazakhstan, and China. The highest peak is Victory Peak at 7,439 meters. The range is part of the Himalayan orogenic belt and features extensive glaciation, such as the 60-km-long Inylchek Glacier. The mountains are a major water source for the arid lowlands, feeding the Syr Darya and Ili rivers. They host significant biodiversity, including snow leopards and argali sheep. The region is also rich in mineral resources like gold and coal.",
